course: dictionary
lesson: 13890
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives kylie two meanings: a curved throwing stick from Australia, and a girl's name. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «The hunter threw the kylie, and it flew low over the grass.» Threw and grass are clues that it is a thrown object, so it must mean the stick.
explain: «Kylie waved at her friend across the playground.» Waved is the clue here. Only a person waves, so Kylie is the name of a person. A capital K at the start of a name is a clue too, but the words around it are the stronger proof.
explain: A good check is to swap in one meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense. Try «The hunter threw the girl's name, and it flew low over the grass.» That does not make sense, so the first meaning is right.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A kylie is a boomerang, especially a non-returning hunting boomerang, a curved throwing stick made by Aboriginal Australians.
fact: «Kylie» is also a girl's name, like the Australian singer Kylie Minogue.
fact: The words around a word show you which meaning is the right one.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so always check the sentence.
exercise: «The hunter threw the kylie, and it flew low over the grass.» What is a kylie in this sentence? | A girl's name | A small red stone | *A boomerang, a curved throwing stick | A kind of bird that sings
exercise: Look at «Kylie waved at her friend across the playground.» What tells you Kylie is a name? | It has the letter K in it | The word playground | It is in the middle of a sentence | *A person waves, so Kylie must be a person
exercise: «The kylie dropped to the ground and did not come back.» Which fact about this kylie is true? | It is a girl's name | It is a kind of song | It came back to the thrower's hand | *It did not return to the thrower
test: «Kylie is my best friend and she lives next door.» What does Kylie mean here? | A type of shoe | A hunting bird | A curved throwing stick | *A girl's name
test: Which of these is a kylie? | *A curved throwing stick made by Aboriginal Australians | A river in Australia | A ball of wool | A teacher at school
exam: Which word in the dictionary entry tells you a kylie is a hunting tool? | singer | name | girl | *hunting
